[333.404, "o", "\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 3 shell commands\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd \"<workspace>\" && python3 -I heatpump_model.py --set scop=4.2 --set gas_kwh=13000 | head -9; p…\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[336.827, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ The stress grid used fixed SCOP values. If you changed your SCOP, the confidence figure would measure the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  wrong thing. I'll centre the grid on your own inputs.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
