[437.495, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 3 report: Depth**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Simulation:** I replaced the hand-picked 54-scenario grid with a seeded simulation of 5,000 draws. It\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  varies efficiency, gas use, installed price, boiler age and cost, fuel price rises, tariff price and VAT\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  together. The ranges are my judgement, centred on your inputs.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Driver ranking:** I added a table that moves each input between plausible extremes and ranks them by how\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  far they move the result.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Self-test:** I built a self-test into the script. It checks the model against Ofgem's £1,723 typical\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  bill, Nesta's published running-cost parity figure, a hand-derived flat-price case, and the rule that better\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  efficiency never hurts. All four pass, and the output is pasted at the bottom of the file.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Standard tariff:** the heat pump is cheaper in only 5% of draws, so the \"no\" verdict is now High\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  confidence (95%). The median is £3,336 worse off.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Heat-pump tariff:** the heat pump is cheaper in 41% of draws, with an 80% range of about £3,260 worse\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  off to £2,300 better off. That's why it stays \"too close\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Biggest drivers:** efficiency, future fuel prices, and the price you pay on a heat-pump tariff move the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  result most. The efficiency and the tariff price are the two you can pin down before buying, so a written\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  efficiency prediction and a quoted tariff would settle most of the uncertainty.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Boiler timing:** this matters more than I'd have guessed. A boiler that fails now turns the heat-pump-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  tariff case from about £50 worse off to about £820 ahead.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed course:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Nesta check:** it first failed by £2 on £950. I traced that to Nesta rounding the price ratio, not a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  model error, and allowed 1% tolerance, labelled in the check.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Verdict wording:** the page-one verdict, bottom line and thresholds are unchanged. Only the confidence\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  figure is now better grounded.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Copies:** I saved the file and script to `.ambition/steps/3/`, leaving `.ambition/first/` untouched.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
