[453.93, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 4/8 · Challenge\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Assumptions I'm resting the verdict on, riskiest first, with who set each one:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | # | Assumption | Set by | Test |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 1 | A \"typical\" home uses 9,500 kWh of gas a year | Me (Ofgem average) | Check against real consumption\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  data for semi-detached homes |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 2 | A heat-pump tariff blends to 20p/kWh | Me | Check against the tariff's published rates |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 3 | SCOP of 3.0 | Me, anchored to Nesta and the field trial | Check against field data and design values |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 4 | Net price £7,500 and a £3,000 replacement boiler | You set the first and I set the second | Check\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  against published installed costs |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 5 | Both fuels rise 3% a year together | Me | Check against forecasts |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 6 | Grant is available and gas can be disconnected cheaply | Me | Check the scheme rules |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I'll start with the first four tests.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
