[644.09, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 5/8 · Range\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What this is really doing, as verbs.** It helps a homeowner **decide** whether to commit about £7,500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  under uncertainty. To do that it has to **answer** the money question, **explain** the answer in plain\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  words, **show** its working so the reader can trust it, **compare** against doing nothing, and **tell them\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  what would change the answer**. Those are the genre's own verbs (a decision memo), and the deliverable stays\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  one Markdown memo.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Fields and what I borrowed from each:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Field | What they actually do | Direction taken |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Decision-memo editor (the genre's best practitioner) | Pre-commit to decision rules before the facts\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  arrive, so a reader can act on them | A **quote test**: grids of efficiency against installed price that say\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  yes / close / no, so the installer's numbers settle it |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Personal-finance adviser | Express an outlay as a rate of return and set it against alternatives | The\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **return on the extra money**, as a yearly percentage |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Insurance actuary | Look at the tails and regret, not just the average | The chance of being more than\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  £2,000 worse off or better off |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Superforecaster (the field I wouldn't normally consider) | Write down dated tripwires that trigger a re-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  forecast | A **when to re-check** list with real dates |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Red team: consumer-protection reviewer | Look for misuse, mis-reading and harm | Tested below by running\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  bad inputs |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The edge I took:** a reader could act on this memo in one sitting. The quote test and the return figure\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  let them judge a real installer quote on the day it arrives.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I'll start with the red team and run some bad inputs against the model.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
