[713.966, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 5 report: Range**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did:** I borrowed one method from each field and applied it to the file, as listed in the table above.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Quote test:** two grids of predicted efficiency against installed price, giving yes / close / no, for a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  standard tariff and for a heat-pump tariff.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Return on the extra money:** a yearly percentage to compare with savings.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Chance of a big loss or gain:** the share of simulated outcomes more than £2,000 worse off or better\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  off.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Dated re-check list:** Ofgem's January cap, the 31 March 2027 VAT end, and boiler failure.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found (red team):**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Crashes:** a zero SCOP, a gas figure below the cooking allowance, a zero horizon and a zero boiler life\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  all crashed with tracebacks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Silent harm:** entering a gas meter's m³ reading as kWh gave a confident \"no\" at 100%, and then crashed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  on an edge case. That is the most likely real-world misuse.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **False precision:** figures like £4,113 implied accuracy the inputs don't have.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Mis-reading:** a \"no\" could be read as \"never\", or applied to homes the model doesn't cover (flats, off-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  gas, Scotland and Wales).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed course:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Input checks:** impossible inputs now stop with a plain message, and odd-looking ones (such as gas under\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  4,000 kWh) get a warning that mentions the ×11.2 m³ conversion.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Rounding:** report figures are rounded (to £50 above £1,000). The pasted script output stays exact.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Scope note:** a note at the top says who the memo is for and who it will mislead.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Verdict:** unchanged. On a standard tariff the extra money loses about 10% a year, and on a heat-pump\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  tariff about 2% a year.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Self-test:** all four checks still pass, and I saved a copy to `.ambition/steps/5/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
