[928.438, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 6 report: Judge**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did:** I built an outside checker, `.ambition/judge/judge.py`, and ran the file through it until it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  passed. It covers:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Independent reimplementation:** a differently written version of the cost model, run on 6 input sets and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  both tariffs.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Structure:** whether the file matches what the script generates, and whether the pasted output is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  verbatim.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Promises:** the original ask and the restatement.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Readability:** word counts per section, jargon, stale text, and contradictions.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Links:** whether each source link loads.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Quote grids:** whether they behave sensibly.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I also gave the file a cold read from top to bottom. It passes all 65 checks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Model bug:** the checker caught an error in the \"installed price needed to break even\" figure, which\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  used a linear shortcut that ignored the remaining-life credit. That figure is now solved properly, and the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  break-even prices rose slightly.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Overstated claims:** I checked three sources I had only seen through search summaries, and each said\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  less than I claimed:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **NEED:** the dataset gives no semi-detached figure.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Carbon Brief:** the article doesn't say the monitor sample is self-selected.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Nesta:** the page doesn't say what I attributed to it about bills.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    I corrected all three. Nesta's parity claim (ratio 3.3, COP 2.8, boiler 85%) is confirmed exactly.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Cold-read issues:** the reader would have hit several things.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Page one:** SCOP and \"heat-pump tariff\" appeared with no gloss.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Contradiction:** the sources section said the grant's end date was unconfirmed while another section\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  stated it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Process leak:** the evidence section said \"my first version\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Page length:** the answer section ran to about 1,030 words.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Repetition and wording:** one sentence repeated itself, and the flip-table cells lacked \"or more\" and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \"or less\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed course:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Page layout:** the quote grids and the re-check list moved out of \"The answer\", which is now about 560\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  words, with page one under 300.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Glossary:** it now covers simulation draws, median, cylinder, SPF and MCS.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Verdict:** unchanged.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Versus the first version:** the first version had no verdict at the top, no source links, no regenerable\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  numbers and only two flagged assumptions. The final has all of those.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Length cost:** the file grew from about 900 to about 4,200 words, but most of that is reference material\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  below the answer.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Not checked:** how a real reader finds the length. I saved a copy to `.ambition/steps/6/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
