[1059.632, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 7 report: Stretch**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did:** I met the stretch target. `python3 heatpump_model.py --me --gas-kwh 12800 --scop 3.4 --price 8200`\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  now gives your own verdict from up to three numbers in about 0.1 seconds. The target was under 10 seconds.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  It accepts gas in m³ (`--gas-m3`) as well as kWh.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Output:** it prints the verdict, the 15-year result on each tariff, how often the heat pump wins across\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the 5,000 simulated futures, and the SCOP and price you'd need to break even.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Where it's documented:** the file's \"Re-run it\" section shows the command.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Fallback:** the `--set` mode, the full report and the earlier steps' checks all still work.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A consistency bug:** the quote grids and the headline verdict used different rules. A quote could be\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \"yes\" in the grid but \"too close\" in the personal verdict. The grids now use the same rule, and the checker\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  confirms all 70 cells match.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Effect on the grids:** they are more cautious. For example, SCOP 3.2 at £5,500 on a standard tariff\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  moved from \"no\" to \"close\". Page one is unchanged.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Cost:** regenerating the full report now takes about 6 seconds instead of 0.1, because every grid cell\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  runs its own simulation. The personal mode is unaffected.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Checker:** it now has 74 checks and all pass. The new ones cover:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - the m³ conversion\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - the speed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - polite refusals of missing, garbage or impossible inputs\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - the warning when m³ is entered as kWh\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Where it would break:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Fixed deals:** the shortcut assumes the Ofgem cap prices. If you're on a fixed deal, you'll need `--set`\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  to enter your own rates.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **The 11.2 m³ conversion:** it is an approximation that varies slightly by supplier.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **SCOP quality:** the verdict is only as good as the SCOP the installer predicts.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Not attempted:** predicting a SCOP from a home's flow temperature. I had no data to check it against.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I saved a copy to `.ambition/steps/7/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
